kunzite: Adreno 710 step 18, GX on through the GMU, slumber in the undo (kgpu=18; 1-17 unchanged).
18 is the second half of the port map's 17: what kgsl does after gen7_hfi_start. First
kgsl_pwrctrl_setup_default_votes: the default perf level (qcom,initial-pwrlevel 7 = 345 MHz, perf
index 10 - 7 - 1 = 2) and the bus level (that level's qcom,bus-freq-ddr7 = 2), each an
H2F_MSG_GX_BW_PERF_VOTE (30; ack_type block; the other field 0xff; no GMU AB vote, so the AB half
is 0xffff). Then gen7_gpu_boot's gen7_gmu_oob_set(oob_gpu): HOST2GMU_INTR_SET bit 30,
GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO bit 31 for up to 100 ms, cleared. GX is judged by GFX_PWR_CLK_STATUS (bit 0 GDSC
off, bit 1 clock off; kgsl gen7_gmu_gx_is_on); only when it says on are RBBM_STATUS, CP_STATUS_1
and CP2GMU_STATUS read (the GPU block's first 16K, mapped here). The undo, in kgsl's power-off
order: the OOB clear (bit 31), then gen7_gmu_power_off: lowest idle (GPU_HW_ACTIVE, IFPC off), the
RSCC's ten TCS DRV0 status bits, H2F_MSG_PREPARE_SLUMBER (33; bw 2, freq 2), fence allow and FAL
next, CX busy bit 30 clear, gen7_rscc_sleep_sequence (CM3 into reset, RSCC_CONTROL_REQ 1, RSCC
STATUS0 bit 16, REQ 0), and if GX still reads on, its GDSC collapsed from here
(gen7_gmu_pwrctrl_suspend's last resort). Two new undo kinds: SLUMBER, and UNMAP for step 17's HFI
alias, which now stays mapped until the undo (pushed before its CM3 entry, so it goes after the
GMU is stopped). The HFI helpers print the running step's number (the slumber message is sent from
the undo).

